{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"999","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Reversing Encryption"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$ can be encrypted by the following algorithm:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" iterate over all divisors of $$$n$$$ in decreasing order (i.e. from $$$n$$$ to $$$1$$$), "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" for each divisor $$$d$$$, reverse the substring $$$s[1 \\dots d]$$$ (i.e. the substring which starts at position $$$1$$$ and ends at position $$$d$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, the above algorithm applied to the string $$$s$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"codeforces"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" leads to the following changes: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"codeforces"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$\\to$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"secrofedoc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$\\to$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"orcesfedoc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$\\to$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"rocesfedoc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$\\to$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"rocesfedoc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (obviously, the last reverse operation doesn't change the string because $$$d=1$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given the encrypted string $$$t$$$. Your task is to decrypt this string, i.e., to find a string $$$s$$$ such that the above algorithm results in string $$$t$$$. It can be proven that this string $$$s$$$ always exists and is unique."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input consists of a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 100$$$) — the length of the string $$$t$$$. The second line of input consists of the string $$$t$$$. The length of $$$t$$$ is $$$n$$$, and it consists only of lowercase Latin letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a string $$$s$$$ such that the above algorithm results in $$$t$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\nrocesfedoc\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"codeforces\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"16\nplmaetwoxesisiht\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"thisisexampletwo\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\nz\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"z\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first example is described in the problem statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"999B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/999/problem/B"}